    "text": "rgb(46, 57, 80)",
    "visibleBody": "ALSO CALLED\nsix-factor matrix\n\nWHAT IT IS\n\nA compact table laying out several factors side by side so their readings can be compared at a glance, rather than read one at a time.\n\nWHY IT MATTERS\n\nSeeing the factors together makes it easier to notice when most of them agree versus when the picture is mixed.\n\nBASIS\nGrid of per-factor state labels\n\nHOW TO READ IT\n\u25b2\nRises\nMost factors pointing the same direction is a more confluent read.\n\u25bc\nFalls\nFactors pointing in different directions is a more mixed, lower-confidence read.\n\u25a0\nSteady\nA mixed matrix is common between regime turns and is not itself a signal to act on.\nWORTH KNOWING\nThe matrix is a coincident read-out, not an independent forecast, and each underlying factor already has its own reference entry.\nWHERE YOU\u2019LL SEE THIS\n\nMacro Dashboard\n\nRELATED\nTrend FactorRisk Appetite FactorVolatility FactorBreadth FactorLiquidity FactorStress Factor\n\nClose",
