    "text": "rgb(46, 57, 80)",
    "visibleBody": "ALSO CALLED\ntrend leg \u00b7 tape trend score\n\nWHAT IT IS\n\nOne of six factors feeding the Market State Score: the multi-timeframe price trend of major US equity indexes, from daily through monthly.\n\nWHY IT MATTERS\n\nConfirms whether the tape's own price action supports the broader market read, weighted toward longer timeframes for durability.\n\nBASIS\n0-100 sub-score (0 = fully risk-off, 100 = fully risk-on)\n\nHOW TO READ IT\n\u25b2\nRises\nHigh score \u2014 trend broadly aligned bullish across timeframes.\n\u25bc\nFalls\nLow score \u2014 trend broadly aligned bearish across timeframes.\n\u25a0\nSteady\nMid score \u2014 short- and longer-term trends disagree.\nWORTH KNOWING\nWeighted toward weekly and monthly timeframes; a strong daily move alone will not move this factor much.\nA trend confirmation measure, not a prediction of the trend's continuation.\nWHERE YOU\u2019LL SEE THIS\n\nMacro Dashboard\n\nRELATED\nMarket State ScoreMarket BreadthRisk Appetite Factor\n\nClose",
